                  <div class="stp-subsection-copy">
                    <p class="stp-keyprinc-p stp-keyprinc-p-1">{{"This is the world we are striving to realize. Our goal is to achieve universal access to"|t}} <span class="stp-keyprinc-tip bb-font" data-tooltip="{{"Sexual and reproductive health is a state of complete physical, mental and social well-being in all matters relating to the reproductive system, the capacity to have a safe and satisfying sex life, the capability to reproduce and the freedom to decide if, when, and how often to do so. It also includes sexual health, the purpose of which is the enhancement of life and personal relations. Reproductive rights include the right of access to sexual and reproductive health information and services, and the right to make decisions concerning reproduction free of discrimination, coercion and violence."|t}}" data-hasqtip="0">{{ 'sexual and reproductive health'|t }}</span>, {{ 'realize reproductive rights, and reduce maternal mortality to accelerate progress on the agenda of the Programme of Action of the'|t }} <span class="stp-keyprinc-tip bb-font" data-tooltip="{{ "The 1994 International Conference on Population and Development (ICPD), held in Cairo, articulated a bold new vision about the relationships between population, development and individual well-being. This vision was embodied in a Programme of Action, which 179 governments adopted and which recognised that reproductive health and rights, and women's empowerment and gender equality, are critical for sustainable development. A major global review of progress in implementing the ICPD Programme of Action 1994-2014 (also analyzing the gaps and challenges that remain) resulted in a Framework of Actions for the follow-up to the Programme of Action of the ICPD."|t }}" data-hasqtip="1">{{ 'International Conference on Population and Development (ICPD)'|t }}</span>, {{ 'to improve the lives of women, adolescents and youth, enabled by population dynamics, human rights and gender equality. Our new strategic plan is designed to drive the ambitions and goals of the ICPD and'|t }} <span class="stp-keyprinc-tip bb-font" data-tooltip="{{ 'The 2030 Agenda is a plan of action for people, planet and prosperity. It forms the new global development framework anchored around 17 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) covering economic and social development, and environmental protection. Poverty eradication is the overarching goal of the new agenda and corresponding Vision 2030 to work together to leave no one behind.'|t }}" data-hasqtip="2">2030&nbsp;{{'agendas'|t}}</span>.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
